Author: Joel <agnel.joel@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 19 03:41:14 2026 -0400

    cuda: cap MMQ Stream-K blocks at available work (#30553)
    
    * cuda: cap Stream-K blocks at the number of k-blocks
    
    Stream-K normally launches one CUDA block per SM. For small matrices,
    this can exceed the total number of output-tile/k-block pairs, leaving
    blocks with no work and adding launch and fixup overhead. Cap the grid
    at that count to remove these excess blocks without changing the useful
    rounded K ranges or numerical results.
    
    Assisted-by: Codex
    
    * cuda: cap Stream-K blocks at the number of k iterations
    
    Cap the grid at the number of K_vram iterations across all output tiles, rounding up partial iterations. This removes extra CUDA blocks left by the k-block cap.
    
    Partial iterations can change FP32 summation grouping. MUL_MAT and MUL_MAT_ID backend tests pass on RTX 5090.
    
    * Update ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Johannes Gäßler <johannesg@5d6.de>

